Z||000000||Pretender||06-20-99||02:33 PM||||whats all involven in a cam upgrade?...does the engine have to be dropped?. i do not plan on doing this my self but i would like to get an idea what the mech. might charge and how many hours it would take. <br>
Z||000001||theogre||06-21-99||12:11 AM||||on a v6 I don't think you can do this w/o removing the engine, or dropping the cradle. On a 4 there should be enough access by dropping the rear of the cradle a couple inches.<p>You'll need to disassemble the motor considerably, you have to replace all the lifters, and all the cam bearings.<p>Unless you are sure the motor is in really good shape, don't just stick a cam in it. Since you will need to strip a good chunk of the motor, now is a good time to have it inspected, and if need be reworked. I know that cost more, but the end result is a much better running motor, and one that will take the abuse you are planning to give it.
